<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/06/18/hero-1781780207418-0e1e8aa8d8.png" alt=""><p class="image-caption"></p></div>
<p id="p2">We’re back with another <a href="https://www.macstories.net/setups/" rel="noopener noreferrer">MacStories Setups update</a>. I swear Federico and I didn’t coordinate our purchases this summer, but you’ll notice that both of us began experimenting with <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6FPNTFM?ref=t_ac_spc_accepted_tile&amp;linkCode=tr1&amp;tag=macstories00-20&amp;linkId=B0H6FPNTFM_1791409739653" rel="noopener noreferrer">XTEINK readers</a> and the <a href="https://repebble.com/index" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pebble Index 01 smart ring</a> without discussing it in advance.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/07/federico-gadgets-composite-v2-1791385988395-6a9dc99fe8.jpg" alt="The UGREEN Thunderbolt 5 Dock and Steam Controller."><p class="image-caption">The UGREEN Thunderbolt 5 Dock and Steam Controller.</p></div>
<p id="p4">Since June, you’ll see from Federico’s changes that many revolve around fine-tuning his app workflows. From re-adding <a href="https://claude.ai/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude</a> and <a href="https://superhuman.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Superhuman</a> to reluctantly adopting <a href="https://www.google.com/chrome/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chrome</a> for agentic workflows, his update reflects a refinement of the way he works. As for gadgets, Federico has begun using the <a href="https://amzn.to/4y21kFC" rel="noopener noreferrer">DJI Mic Mini</a> and <a href="https://repebble.com/index" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pebble Index 01</a> for dictation and refined his work and gaming desktop setup with a <a href="https://amzn.to/4y1jGq8" rel="noopener noreferrer">UGREEN Thunderbolt 5 dock</a> and <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/hardware/steamcontroller" rel="noopener noreferrer">Steam Controller</a>.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/07/john-gadgets-composite-v2-1791385989746-074dbf82de.jpg" alt="The XTEINK 4 Pro and Retroid Pocket Nova."><p class="image-caption">The XTEINK 4 Pro and Retroid Pocket Nova.</p></div>
<p id="p6">My setup changes this summer revolve around experiments. I first tried the <a href="https://amzn.to/4y2SDL9" rel="noopener noreferrer">XTEINK 3 reader</a> and enjoyed creating a custom UI for it so much that I also bought the <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6FPNTFM?ref=t_ac_spc_accepted_tile&amp;linkCode=tr1&amp;tag=macstories00-20&amp;linkId=B0H6FPNTFM_1791409739653" rel="noopener noreferrer">XTEINK 4 Pro</a>, which is patiently waiting for a free weekend when I can see what more I can do with it. Plus I’ve been trying a bunch of new apps like <a href="https://t3.codes/" rel="noopener noreferrer">T3 Code</a> for working with multiple AI subscriptions, <a href="https://openminis.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Minis</a> to get more out of iOS than Siri AI allows, and working with a wide variety of remote access apps, including <a href="https://excbadacc.es/beam" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beam</a> and <a href="https://jumpdesktop.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jump Desktop</a>. Finally, I’ve partially abandoned my custom social media web apps for <a href="https://typefully.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Typefully</a>, which has more features than I’d ever want to build myself.</p>
<p id="p7">That’s it for this edition of Setups. Be sure to check out the links here and on the <a href="https://www.macstories.net/setups/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Setups page</a> because some of these gadgets are on sale on Amazon for its Prime Big Deal Days event. Also, be sure to follow the MacStories Deals social media accounts on <a href="https://x.com/MacStoriesDeals" rel="noopener noreferrer">X.com</a>, <a href="https://mastodon.macstories.net/@MacStoriesDeals" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mastodon</a>, and <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/macstoriesdeals.macstories.net" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluesky</a>.</p>
